# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: windows-ssh-build-lacks-appdata — make over ssh on Windows dies loading Quicklisp: Invalid pathname #P"config/"
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: fix-windows-ssh-appdata-defaults
#+DATE: 2026-11-15

* Symptom

=ssh pfenny ./update-clautolisp= (a =git pull= then =make=) fails at the
first Lisp the build starts, =build-read-autolisp-sbcl=, while loading
=quicklisp/setup.lisp=:

#+begin_example
Unhandled SIMPLE-ERROR ...
  Invalid pathname #P"config/": Expected an absolute pathname
4: (UIOP/PATHNAME:ENSURE-PATHNAME #P"config/" ... :WANT-ABSOLUTE T ...)
5: (UIOP/CONFIGURATION:RESOLVE-ABSOLUTE-LOCATION (#P"config/" ((#P"common-lisp/source-registry.conf"))) ...)
6: (UIOP/CONFIGURATION:XDG-CONFIG-PATHNAMES #P"common-lisp/source-registry.conf")
#+end_example

The same update on poseidon and thalassa succeeds.

* Cause

Not the code being built: the environment. An OpenSSH-for-Windows session
into MSYS2 carries none of =USERPROFILE=, =LOCALAPPDATA=, =APPDATA= (they come
from the interactive logon profile). On Windows UIOP computes

#+begin_src lisp
(xdg-config-home) = (or $XDG_CONFIG_HOME (xdg-data-home "config/"))
(xdg-data-home)   = (or $XDG_DATA_HOME (get-folder-path :local-appdata))
;; :local-appdata = (or $LOCALAPPDATA (subpathname $APPDATA "Local"))
#+end_src

so with all of them unset the base is NIL and the result is the relative
=#P"config/"=, which =resolve-absolute-location= rejects (uiop 3.3.6,
=configuration.lisp= =xdg-config-home=). Every SBCL started from that shell
fails the same way.

The CI Windows lanes never hit it: they source
=scripts/environnement-windows.sh=, which sets the three when absent. The
Makefiles did not.

* Fix

=scripts/windows-environment.mk=, included by every Makefile that starts a
Lisp (root, =clautolisp=, =autolisp-front-end=, =autolisp-test=,
=autolisp-benchmark=). On Windows (=OS=Windows_NT=, or =uname -s= MINGW* /
MSYS* / CYGWIN*) it exports, only when missing, =USERPROFILE= =
=C:/Users/<user>=, =LOCALAPPDATA= = =$USERPROFILE/AppData/Local=,
=APPDATA= = =$USERPROFILE/AppData/Roaming= -- the values the interactive
session has, so UIOP finds the same configuration. The user name is not
trusted from one variable, since over ssh =USERNAME= is usually absent and
=USER= may be the login form (=domain+user=): the candidates =USERNAME=,
=USER=, =LOGNAME= and the last component of =HOME= are tried, and the first
whose =C:/Users/<name>= folder exists wins (else the first candidate). Existing values are never
overridden and no mixed-case twin is created.

Regression test: =scripts/tests/test-windows-environment-mk.sh=
(=make check-windows-make-environment=, part of =make check-release=): the
fragment's behaviour on a simulated Windows / Unix shell, and the include in
each of the five Makefiles.

* Resolved

clautolisp / alfe 2.4.11 (2026-11-15). Verified by the regression test on
macOS with simulated Windows environments (domain-style =USER=, =HOME= only,
existing values, no user). The MR is merged only after the build has been
re-run over ssh on pfenny, whose sshd stopped answering the banner during
the investigation.
